# GD-24 (round 19, writer 10): settled; was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §2.4. L §2.4: "At one key position the wider key comes first: `*` before every other key".
# The old comment:
# L §2.4 sorts version items "then keys in index order (things and an open index's keys in the text order of their
# stable ids, §2.5)"; a `*` (every key, §4.6) is no key of the index, and the section gives it no place among them:
# REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED (the order of pay[*] and pay[ola] decides the canonical text, so the hash).
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

kind persons
input pay[p in persons]: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  pay[ola] = 2 PLN
  pay[*] = 1 PLN
